DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aaccll__ddeelleettee__ddeeff__ffiillee(), aaccll__ddeelleettee__ddeeff__lliinnkk__nnpp(), aaccll__ddeelleettee__ffdd__nnpp(),
     aaccll__ddeelleettee__ffiillee__nnpp(), and aaccll__ddeelleettee__lliinnkk__nnpp() each allow the deletion of
     an ACL from a file.  The aaccll__ddeelleettee__ddeeff__ffiillee() function is a POSIX.1e
     call that deletes the default ACL from a file (normally a directory) by
     name; the remainder of the calls are non-portable extensions that permit
     the deletion of arbitrary ACL types from a file/directory either by path
     name or file descriptor.  The __ffiillee() variations follow a symlink if it
     occurs in the last segment of the path name; the __lliinnkk() variations oper‐
     ate on the symlink itself.

